<Project>
  <!--
    **The shield.** MSBuild walks up from a project directory and stops at the
    first `Directory.Build.props` it finds, so this empty file is what keeps
    `plugins/Directory.Build.props` — our target framework, our
    CounterStrikeSharp pin, `TreatWarningsAsErrors` — off the vendored trees
    below it. They are stock, pinned and never patched (docs/pins.md): they
    build with the properties upstream wrote and against the package versions
    upstream chose, and a warning in somebody else's source is not ours to
    fail a build over.

    Nothing here is in `plugins/EZPug.sln`, so `pnpm verify`'s
    `dotnet build -warnaserror` never sees it either; `plugins/vendor/build.sh`
    is the one thing that builds it, and `docker/cs2/Dockerfile` is the one
    thing that calls that.
  -->
</Project>
